<title>INDIA: Capital adequacy ratios of Indian state-run banks.</title>
<headline>Capital adequacy ratios of Indian state-run banks.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a table of capital adequacy ratios of India's public sector (state-run) banks prepared by securities firm HG Asia (Hoare Govett (India) Securities Ltd.</p>
<p>	 CAPITAL ADEQUACY RATIOS IN PERCENTAGE</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Bank					 FY95	 FY96</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Oriental Bank of Commerce	    18.7	 17.0</p>
<p>State Bank of Saurashtra *	    5.2	 12.4</p>
<p>State Bank of India		    12.8	 11.6</p>
<p>Bank of Baroda			    8.7	 11.2</p>
<p>Corporation Bank			 10.7	 11.1</p>
<p>Canara Bank				10.4	 10.4</p>
<p>Allahabad Bank			    4.9	 10.1</p>
<p>State Bank of Hyderabad *	     6.6	  9.9</p>
<p>State Bank of Patialia *	     10.0	  9.5</p>
<p>Union Bank of India		     8.3	  9.5</p>
<p>State Bank of Tranvancore *	   3.1	  9.4</p>
<p>State Bank of Bikaner &amp; Jaipur *    4.2	  9.3</p>
<p>State Bank of Indore *		  5.1	  8.8</p>
<p>State Bank of Mysore *		  3.6	  8.8</p>
<p>Bank of Maharashtra		     6.0	  8.5</p>
