<p># Indicates negative figures</p>
<p>* Associate Banks of SBI</p>
<p>As per the capital adequacy norms prescribed by the Reserve Bank of India, all Indian banks with international operations had to achieve a capital adequacy ratio (CAR) of eight percent by March 1995, while the other Indian banks had to do so by March 1996.</p>
<p>To help the banks achieve the capital adequacy norms, the government infused fresh capital into loss-making banks. Over the past three years, the government has provided an estimated 118.4 billion rupees towards recapitalistion of banks.</p>
